        "body": "<i>Imported from JIRA <a href=\"https://jira.lyrasis.org/browse/DS-4070\">[DS-4070]</a> created by mwood</i>\n<p>There is a feature which enables one to request a copy of an Item which is access-restricted.  These requests are stored in the database until they are resolved.  The database record is never deleted, and in fact the DAO has no method for doing so.</p>\n\n<p>Was this a conscious decision, to retain requests forever?  Should requests be deletable? should they be deleted mechanically? when?</p>\n\n<p>It should be noted that copy request records necessarily contain personally identifying information, and thus retention policy may need review with respect to laws regarding such information.</p>",
